# Large binaries: store with Git LFS (run `git lfs install` once per machine, then commit as usual).
# GitHub Pages serves the git tree as static files and does not expand LFS pointers. For Pages, either
# use a deploy workflow with `lfs: true` and a step that materializes files, or host heavy MP4s on a CDN
# (e.g. media.githubusercontent.com) and link those URLs in HTML.
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Keep this hero asset as a normal blob so GitHub Pages always serves the real GIF bytes.
img/TIT/TIT_Gameplay.gif -filter -diff -merge
